{title: Silent Night}
{subtitle: Stille Nacht}
{artist: Joseph Mohr}
{composer: Franz Xaver Gruber}
{key: G}
{time: 6/8}
{tempo: 60}
{tags: Christmas, Worship, Traditional, Carol}
{copyright: Public Domain}
{year: 1818}

{comment: Gentle, peaceful carol - play softly}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Silent night, holy night!
[D]All is calm, [G]all is bright.
[C]Round yon Virgin, [G]Mother and Child.
[C]Holy infant so [G]tender and mild,
[D]Sleep in heavenly [Em]peace,
[G]Sleep in [D]heavenly [G]peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Silent night, holy night!
[D]Shepherds quake [G]at the sight.
[C]Glories stream from [G]heaven afar
[C]Heavenly hosts sing [G]Alleluia,
[D]Christ the Savior is [Em]born!
[G]Christ the [D]Savior is [G]born.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Silent night, holy night!
[D]Son of God, [G]love's pure light.
[C]Radiant beams from [G]Thy holy face
[C]With the dawn of re[G]deeming grace,
[D]Jesus, Lord at Thy [Em]birth,
[G]Jesus, [D]Lord at Thy [G]birth.
{end_of_verse}
